==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|ars}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*arsaz}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*h₃érsos||behind, arse}}. Compare {{cog|nl|aars}}, {{cog|en|arse}}, {{cog|no|rass}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʔaʁʃ/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/ʔaːʃ/|lang=de}} {{a|widespread, especially northern and central Germany}}
* {{audio|De-Arsch.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Arsches|gen2=Arschs|Ärsche}}

# {{lb|de|vulgar}} [[arse]], [[posterior]], [[buttocks]]

====Usage notes====
* In formal settings, ''Arsch'' is vulgar and inappropriate; in informal settings (e.g. among friends or family) this is often not the case. Note, however, that ''Arsch'' may have a stronger sexual implication than some synonyms, which—in certain contexts—might make the word inappropriate even in very informal settings.

